---
/**
 * Privacy policy — English translation of the adapted German version
 * (/datenschutz). The German version is the legally authoritative one; the
 * layout renders that notice automatically.
 */
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { translatePath } from "../../lib/i18n";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for kandzior.de: no cookies, no tracking, embeds load only after an explicit click."
  lang="en"
  altPath={translatePath("/en/privacy", "de")}
  stand="Last updated: August 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller within the meaning of the General Data Protection
    Regulation (GDPR) and other national data protection laws of the member
    states as well as other data protection provisions is:
  </p>
  <address>
    Martin Kandzior<br />
    Theodor-Heuss-Anlage 12<br />
    68165 Mannheim, Germany<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:mail@kandzior.de">mail@kandzior.de</a><br />
    Phone: <a href="tel:+4917610202030">+49 176 10 20 20 30</a>
  </address>

  <h2>2. The essentials first</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies, uses no analytics or tracking services, and
    loads no content from third-party servers when you open it. A connection
    to a third party is only ever established when you actively trigger it
    yourself with an explicit click (sections 6 and 7).
  </p>

  <h2>3. Provision of the website and log files (hosting)</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted by an external service provider (Hetzner Online
    GmbH, Industriestr. 25, 91710 Gunzenhausen, Germany). Personal data
    collected on this website is stored on the host's servers exclusively
    within the Federal Republic of Germany.
  </p>
  <p>
    On every visit, the system automatically collects data and information
    from the visiting device:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>IP address of the requesting device</li>
    <li>date and time of access</li>
    <li>name and URL of the retrieved file</li>
    <li>website from which access was made (referrer URL)</li>
    <li>browser used and, where applicable, operating system and access provider</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR. My legitimate interest lies in
    the technically sound presentation and optimisation of my website and in
    safeguarding the security of the IT systems. The data is deleted as soon
    as it is no longer required for the purpose of its collection; storage in
    log files beyond that occurs for a limited period for security reasons. A
    data processing agreement pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR is in place with
    Hetzner.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Local storage of preferences</h2>
  <p>
    When you switch the appearance (light/dark) or the language, your choice
    is stored in your browser's local storage so it is preserved on your next
    visit. This information remains entirely on your device, is never
    transmitted to me or to third parties, and contains no personal data.
    Storage is necessary for the service you requested (§ 25 (2) no. 2
    TDDDG). You can delete it at any time via your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Contact form</h2>
  <p>
    This website contains a contact form for electronic contact. If you use
    it, the data entered in the form (name, email address, message text) is
    transmitted to me and processed solely to handle your enquiry. It is not
    passed on to third parties.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR; where the contact aims at
    concluding a contract, additionally Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR. The data is
    deleted once the respective conversation has ended and the circumstances
    indicate that the matter in question has been conclusively resolved. You
    may object to the processing at any time; an informal message to
    <a href="mailto:mail@kandzior.de">mail@kandzior.de</a> suffices. As an
    alternative to the form, you can always reach me directly by email.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Embedded social network content (two-click solution)</h2>
  <p>
    Content from LinkedIn (LinkedIn Ireland Unlimited Company), X (X Corp.)
    and Facebook (Meta Platforms Ireland Ltd.) can be embedded on this
    website. Merely opening the page establishes <strong>no</strong>
    connection to these providers. Instead of the content, you first see a
    preview served entirely from my own server.
  </p>
  <p>
    Only when you click "Load posts" is a direct connection established
    between your device and the servers of the respective provider. In doing
    so, your IP address and the information that you visited this page are
    transmitted to the provider. If you are logged in there, the provider can
    associate the visit with your account. The legal basis is your consent
    declared by the click (Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR in conjunction with § 25 (1)
    TDDDG). The consent applies to that page view; reloading the page ends
    it, and no further connection is made without another click.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use of these services may involve data transfers to the USA and other
    third countries. The providers rely on standard contractual clauses or,
    where available, on certification under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy
    Framework. For details, see the providers' privacy policies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      LinkedIn:
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
        >linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      X: <a href="https://x.com/en/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">x.com/en/privacy</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Facebook:
      <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
        >facebook.com/privacy/policy</a
      >
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where this site merely links to my profiles, no data is exchanged with
    the respective provider when the page is opened. Only when you click the
    link are you taken to the platform, where the provider's privacy policy
    applies.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Events (Ticket Tailor)</h2>
  <p>
    For displaying and booking events I use Ticket Tailor (Zimma Ltd, United
    Kingdom). The two-click rule applies here as well: opening the page
    establishes no connection to Ticket Tailor; only your click on "Load
    events" does, transmitting your IP address in the process (Art. 6 (1) (a)
    GDPR in conjunction with § 25 (1) TDDDG). An adequacy decision of the
    European Commission is in place for the United Kingdom.
  </p>
  <p>
    Registration and, where applicable, payment take place entirely on Ticket
    Tailor's pages; this website neither stores nor processes any of your
    data in that process. Ticket Tailor's
    <a href="https://www.tickettailor.com/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
      >privacy policy</a
    > applies.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Rights of the data subject</h2>
  <p>As a data subject, you have the following rights:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Right of access</strong> (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Right to restriction of processing</strong> (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Right to object</strong> to processing based on Art. 6 (1) (f)
      GDPR (Art. 21 GDPR)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Right to withdraw consent</strong> with effect for the future
      (Art. 7 (3) GDPR)
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    An informal message to
    <a href="mailto:mail@kandzior.de">mail@kandzior.de</a> suffices to
    exercise these rights.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority</h2>
  <p>
    Without prejudice to any other administrative or judicial remedy, you
    have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory
    authority, in particular in the member state of your habitual residence,
    your place of work or the place of the alleged infringement.
  </p>
  <p>The authority responsible for me as controller based in Mannheim is:</p>
  <address>
    Der Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit
    Baden-Württemberg (LfDI)<br />
    Postfach 10 29 32<br />
    70025 Stuttgart, Germany<br />
    <a
      href="https://www.baden-wuerttemberg.datenschutz.de"
      rel="noopener"
      target="_blank">baden-wuerttemberg.datenschutz.de</a
    >
  </address>

  <h2>10. SSL/TLS encryption</h2>
  <p>
    For security reasons and to protect the transmission of confidential
    content, this site uses SSL/TLS encryption. You can recognise an
    encrypted connection by the browser address line changing from "http://"
    to "https://" and by the lock symbol in your browser bar.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Validity and changes to this privacy policy</h2>
  <p>
    This privacy policy is currently valid (last updated: August 2026).
    Further development of my website and services or changed legal or
    official requirements may make it necessary to amend this privacy policy.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
